cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MACE or MACE-Bench, please cite this repository and the accompanying paper."
title: "MACE: Masking-Aware Counterfactual Exploration with Executable Verification"
abstract: >-
  MACE is an LLM-guided, source-grounded framework for discovering and
  verifying minimal masking explanations through executable counterfactual
  interventions. This repository contains the MACE engine, the MACE-Bench
  v2.1 dataset, the Graph/AST-only baseline (C0), the LLM-guided Full MACE
  pipeline, the Direct LLM baselines, and the frozen results reported in the
  paper.
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-06"
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "MACE Authors"
keywords:
  - program comprehension
  - counterfactual execution
  - masking relations
  - minimality verification
  - LLM-guided program analysis
  - benchmark
